00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.636
AUBREY PLAZA:
<i> Isn't it just crazy
 that you're in the cast,</i>

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.538
<i> and you're in this hit show.</i>

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.140
I guess. Is it crazy for you?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.141
I'm not even here.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.776
You have to answer
some questions.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.243
I'm the interviewer.

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:13.246
That's not--
That's not correct.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.782
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:24.156
Episode two, Harper and Ethan
have dinner with Cameron
and Daphne.

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:26.492 line:0%
And they get into a conversation
about having kids.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.295
And I think it kind of
catches them off guard
a little bit.

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.697
Do you want to have kids?

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.133
Uh...

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.502
They kind of touch a nerve
without realizing,

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.938
by asking us about, like,
our sex life.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.007
And where we're saying,
"I know we're fine."

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.343
We do it, you know,
enough, like...

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.713
We think we're good,
and then by the end of dinner,

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.048
I'm like, "Oh.
Maybe we're not."

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:50.950
The problem is, I'm more of
a morning sex guy,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.019
and Harper is not
a morning person.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.287
DAPHNE SULLIVAN:
Hm, yeah. Makes sense.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.156
I don't want to make this
like a therapy session for us.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.123
WILL SHARPE: Okay.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.327
I would say the root of
the tension between
Harper and Ethan,

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:04.697
in my opinion, and sweetheart,
you can say whatever you want.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:05.698
Uh-huh.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.400
But there's like this
underlying resentment

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.337
that is kind of building
towards Ethan for her.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:12.972
ETHAN SPILLER: Why are you
threatened by them?

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.139
HARPER SPILLER: I'm not.

00:01:14.606 --> 00:01:16.842
I was just trying to say I think
we have a good relationship,

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:18.211
but I won't do that again.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.580
There's this false belief
that if you go on vacation,

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.415
-you leave your life behind.
-Leave all your problems behind.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.852
And you actually
are just the same person,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:26.852
living the same life.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.955
And all your problems
go with you.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.823
<i> It doesn't matter
 what the view is,</i>

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:31.957
you're never gonna be happy.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.259
Aubrey.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.460
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.663
How do you guys like being rich?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.697
Oh, Cameron. God.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:38.798
Come on.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.067
It probably effects
your sense of self

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.602
to have recently come
into a lot of money.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:46.673
I don't feel like that's what
the problem is with
Ethan and Harper.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.175
I almost feel like they are
exactly how they were

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:50.609
when they didn't have
as much money.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:54.146
Except, they're in
a different place,
with different people.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.883
And maybe that's the catalyst
for all the other stuff

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.083
to kind of bubble out.

00:01:58.183 --> 00:01:59.518
I had to have
an emergency caesarean.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.887
Daphne's guts were all over
the table, you know.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:05.658
Daphne and Cameron
have this like really
tender moment about their kids.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:08.728
And I think it's like the first
time Harper feels like,

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.364
"Maybe I've really
judged them harshly."

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.902
It's in those moments,
you realize just how much
you love somebody, you know?

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.171
I love you.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.606
AUBREY:<i> And also, maybe they
 have it all figured out,</i>

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:26.245
and I'm just some stuck-up bitch
that has a stick up my ass.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.381
-Can I say that on HBO?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.556
I would pick Tanya
